{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"Effects have a different lifecycle from components.","source_span":"Effects have a different lifecycle from components."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"A component mounts when it's added to the screen.","source_span":"A component _mounts_ when it's added to the screen."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"A component updates when it receives new props or state, usually in response to an interaction.","source_span":"A component _updates_ when it receives new props or state, usually in response to an interaction."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"A component unmounts when it's removed from the screen.","source_span":"A component _unmounts_ when it's removed from the screen."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"An Effect can only do two things: start synchronizing something, and later stop synchronizing it.","source_span":"An Effect can only do two things: to start synchronizing something, and later to stop synchronizing it."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"React provides a linter rule to check that Effect dependencies are specified correctly.","source_span":"React provides a linter rule to check that you've specified your Effect's dependencies correctly."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"If an Effect doesn't return a cleanup function, React behaves as if it returned an empty cleanup function.","source_span":"if you don't, React will behave as if you returned an empty cleanup function."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"In the ChatRoom example, the serverUrl is set to 'https://localhost:1234'.","source_span":"const serverUrl = 'https://localhost:1234';"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","statement":"When roomId changes, React first stops synchronizing with the old roomId (disconnects from the \"general\" room) then starts synchronizing with the new roomId (connects to the \"travel\" room).","source_span":"1. Stop synchronizing with the old `roomId` (disconnect from the `\"general\"` room)\n2. Start synchronizing with the new `roomId` (connect to the `\"travel\"` room)"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","fact_refs":[4],"question":"According to the React docs, what are the only two things an Effect's lifecycle can do?","answer":"An Effect can only start synchronizing something, and later stop synchronizing it — unlike components, which mount, update, and unmount."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What is the initial value of serverUrl in the ChatRoom Effect example?","answer":"'https://localhost:1234'"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","fact_refs":[8],"question":"What happens when the roomId prop in the ChatRoom example changes from \"general\" to \"travel\"?","answer":"React first stops synchronizing by calling the cleanup function to disconnect from the \"general\" room, then starts synchronizing by running the Effect again to connect to the \"travel\" room."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What does React do if an Effect doesn't return a cleanup function?","answer":"React behaves as if you had returned an empty cleanup function."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","fact_refs":[3],"question":"When does a component unmount, according to the lifecycle of reactive effects doc?","answer":"A component unmounts when it's removed from the screen."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_lifecycle-of-reactive-effects","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What tool does React provide to check that you've specified an Effect's dependencies correctly?","answer":"React provides a linter rule for checking that Effect dependencies are specified correctly."}
